From: Elian Doran <doran.adoris.elian@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] clk: sunxi-ng: a64: pll-mipi leaves pll-video0's rate alone

pll-video0 feeds pll-mipi (the DSI panel's TCON0) and HDMI (its PHY clock
and TCON1 divide it). pll-mipi set its parent's rate for the panel: 250 MHz
on the PinePhone, from which no CEA mode divides, and the panel holds the
rate exclusively. The board now fixes pll-video0 (297 MHz, assigned in the
device tree) and pll-mipi makes the panel's rate from it. The panel's mode
(69 MHz, 24 bpp over 4 lanes) asks 414 MHz, 55.3 Hz; the 500 MHz minimum
(the user manual's) made it 500 before, 66.8 Hz, which phone-ui was tuned
at. From 297 MHz, 500 is not made: the minimum is now 495 (297 x 5 / 3),
which pll-mipi makes exactly, 66.1 Hz.

---
--- a/drivers/clk/sunxi-ng/ccu-sun50i-a64.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/sunxi-ng/ccu-sun50i-a64.c
@@ -180,11 +180,22 @@
 	.min_parent_m_ratio	= 24000000,
 	.common		= {
 		.reg		= 0x040,
+		/*
+		 * Not CLK_SET_RATE_PARENT: pll-video0 also feeds HDMI (its PHY
+		 * and TCON1 divide it), which needs it at 297 MHz (the board's
+		 * assigned-clock-rates) for the CEA modes. pll-mipi makes the
+		 * panel's rate from what it is.
+		 */
 		.hw.init	= CLK_HW_INIT("pll-mipi", "pll-video0",
 					      &ccu_nkm_ops,
-					      CLK_SET_RATE_UNGATE | CLK_SET_RATE_PARENT),
+					      CLK_SET_RATE_UNGATE),
 		.features	= CCU_FEATURE_CLOSEST_RATE,
-		.min_rate	= 500000000,
+		/*
+		 * The user manual says 500 MHz, which pll-video0 at 297 does not
+		 * make: 495 (x 5 / 3). The PinePhone panel's mode asks 414 (55 Hz),
+		 * raised to this minimum: 66 Hz, as it ran at 500.
+		 */
+		.min_rate	= 495000000,
 		.max_rate	= 1400000000,
 	},
 };
